        "smuflSuccessorFont": "Bravura",
        "successorNotes": "A deliberate substitution, not a design successor. Sibelius never supported SMuFL, so Opus has no SMuFL descendant. Bravura is named because the OFL font Norfolk is Bravura reconfigured onto the Opus character layout, making it the established modern stand-in for Opus.",
        "staffSpacesPerEm": 4.0,
        "sizeNotes": "Measured against Bravura on single-symbol anchors (cClef 4.03, accidentalSharp 4.06, accidentalFlat 4.08); notehead comparison against Leland and Finale Maestro corroborates 3.95-4.06 after correcting for notehead overshoot. Clefs and time-signature digits scatter 3.7-4.3, the expected signature of an independently drawn design."
